s","count":1},{"gloss":"espantaram","count":1},{"gloss":"se-espantavam","count":1}]},"G2319":{"id":"G2319","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2319","disambiguated_id":"G2319 =","unique_id":"G2319","headword":"θεοστυγής","transliteration":"theostugēs","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"God-hating","definition_en":"θεοστυγής, -ές\n (θεός, στυγέω), \n__1. passive, as frequently in cl., hateful to God: Rom.1:30 (R, txt., cf. Lit., Notes, 256). \n __2. Active, hating God: lb. (R, mg., cf. ICC, in l).†\n (AS)","source_line":2468}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"difamadores","count":1}]},"G2325":{"id":"G2325","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2325","disambiguated_id":"G2325 =","unique_id":"G2325","headword":"θερίζω","transliteration":"therizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to reap","definition_en":"θερίζω\n (θέρος), [in LXX chiefly for קָצַר ;] \nto reap: Mat.6:26, Luk.12:24, Jas.5:4; figuratively, Mat.25:24, 26, Luk.19:21-22, Jhn.4:36-38, 2Co.9:6, Gal.6:7, 9, Rev.14:15; with accusative, τ. σαρκικά, 1Co.9:11; φθοράν, ζωὴν αἰώνιον, Gal.6:8; τ. γῆν, Rev.14:16.†\n (AS)","source_line":2474}],"occurrence_count":21,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"colherá","count":5},{"gloss":"ceifa","count":4},{"gloss":"ceifam","count":2},{"gloss":"colhes","count":2},{"gloss":"colho","count":2},{"gloss":"ceifar","count":2},{"gloss":"colhermos","count":1},{"gloss":"colheremos","count":1},{"gloss":"colheita","count":1},{"gloss":"ceifada","count":1}]},"G2387":{"id":"G2387","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2387","disambiguated_id":"G2387 =","unique_id":"G2387","headword":"Ἰαμβρῆς","transliteration":"Iambrēs","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Jambres","definition_en":"Ἰαμβρῆς, ὁ \n Jambres (cf. Exo.7:11-12): 2Ti.3:8.†\n (AS)","source_line":2540}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Jambres","count":1}]},"G2398":{"id":"G2398","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2398","disambiguated_id":"G2398 =","unique_id":"G2398","headword":"ἴδιος","transliteration":"idios","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"one's own/private","definition_en":"ἴδιος, -α, -ον (in Attic usually -ος, -ον), \n [in LXX chiefly for of person(s) suff., also for לָהֶם, etc.; (τὰ ἴ.) בֵּיתוֹ ;] \n __1. one's own; \n__(a) of that which is private and personal (in cl. opposite to κοινός, δημόσιος; cf. infr. 3); \n __(b) of property, friends, home, country, etc. (in cl. opposite to ἀλλότριος; in late writers often, like ἑαυτοῦ, with weakened sense, see M, Pr., 87ff.; Deiss., BS, 123f.): Luk.6:41, Jhn.1:42 5:43, Act.2:6 20:28, 1Co.11:21, Gal.6:5, 2Ti.1:9, Heb.7:27, Ju 6, al.; πράσσειν τὰ ἴ., 1Th.4:11; κατὰ τὰς ἰ. ἐπιθυμίας, 2Ti.4:3; οἱ ἴδιοι, Jhn.1:11 (M, Pr., 90f.; Field, Notes, 84) 13:1, Act.4:23, 1Ti.5:8; τὰ ἴδια, one's home (Field, Notes, l.with), Luk.18:28, Jhn.1:11 16:32 19:27. \n __2. peculiar, distinct, appropriate, proper: τὸ ἴ. σῶμα, 1Co.15:38; ἐν τ. ἰ. τάγματι, 1Co.15:23; εἰς τ. τόπον τ. ἴ., Act.1:25; = αὐτοῦ (see Deiss., ut. supr.), Mat.22:5, Jhn.1:42 (cf. Wis.10:1). \n __3. Adverbially (see supr., 1 (a); and cf. WM, 739:2); \n__(a) ἰδίᾳ, severally, separately: 1Co.12:11; \n __(b) κατ᾽ ἰδίαν, apart, privately, in private: Mat.14:13, 23 20:17, Mrk.4:34 7:33, Luk.10:23, Act.23:19, al.\n (AS)","source_line":2551}],"occurrence_count":114,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"próprio","count":24},{"gloss":"própria","count":22},{"gloss":"parte","count":11},{"gloss":"seus","count":9},{"gloss":"próprios","count":8},{"gloss":"próprias","count":5},{"gloss":"particular","count":4},{"gloss":"seu","count":4},{"gloss":"sua","count":4},{"gloss":"suas","count":3},{"gloss":"seu-próprio","count":3},{"gloss":"sua-própria","count":2},{"gloss":"devido","count":2},{"gloss":"seus-próprios","count":2},{"gloss":"sozinho","count":1},{"gloss":"reservadamente","count":1},{"gloss":"próprias-coisas","count":1},{"gloss":"casa","count":1},{"gloss":"companheiros","count":1},{"gloss":"suas-coisas","co